From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] cover inlined and preload BZI6 legacy mapper guards

# Reason: actual0193 trial still aborts inside GraphicBuffer constructor because compiler inlined a second API>35 guard; preloadHal also gates the same retained mapper2/3 path. Whole-executable call-site audit finds exactly three relevant API calls, not one.
# Affected: M4 runtime helper/lock only. Cover all three decoded B.GT branches with per-site executable-segment/context/target and whole-file hashes; existing restore/image metadata gates consume the new output hash.
# Verify: scan all executable BL call sites to the actual API-level PLT; require all three API35 guards covered; only12 instruction bytes differ and all mapper load/allocator checks remain; helper/real-ext4 fixture and full184-patch replay. Record runtime separately.
# Rollback: reverse0194 and lock/series entry, or restore original libui in the bounded device test;0193 is retained as an insufficient historical diagnostic. No OS property, HAL, kernel, radio or EFS change.

